[00:10.60]For his age, he's wise
[00:15.26]He's got his mother's eyes
[00:19.76]There's gladness in his heart
[00:22.02]He's young and he's wild
[00:29.34]My only prayer is, if I can't be there
[00:39.76]Lord, protect my child
[00:46.60]As his youth now unfolds
[00:50.84]He is centuries old
[00:57.26]See him at play makes me smile
[01:04.30]No matter what happens to me
[01:08.22]No matter what my destiny
[01:14.86]Lord, protect my child
[01:21.72]Well, the whole world is asleep
[01:25.92]You can look at it and weep
[01:30.84]Few things you find are worthwhile
[01:39.08]And though I don't ask for much
[01:43.22]No material things to touch
[01:49.16]Lord, protect my child
[01:56.92]He's young and on fire
[01:58.28]Full of hope and desire
[02:02.90]In a world that's been raped, raped and defiled
[02:14.12]If I fall along the way
[02:17.98]And can't see another day
[02:23.53]Lord, protect my child
[03:05.90]There'll be a time I hear tell
[03:10.32]When all will be well
[03:14.66]When God and man will be reconciled
[03:23.16]But until men lose their chains
[03:27.26]And righteousness reigns
[03:30.66]Lord, protect my child
